Z||000012||Archie||05-28-2001||01:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by saleenfiero:<BR><B>What the hel! do people expect, a convertable conversion for $200?  Sure if you get a paper top and a hacksaw.  It take ballz to take a gamble and see if something sells.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>When these kits were being sold by Fred, they were between $2700 and $3500 depending on options & how bad Fred needed the $ that week  etc. They were all handbuilt one at a time.<P>The parts I just got on EBay include the frame stiffener, the windshield header parts and the fender caps.<P>If I got into this, I'd be wanting to sell 50 units a year at a price ~$2000.<P>That's a tall order but mass production should help keep the price down.<P>I hear that Fred is currently living in the Chicago area, maybe this discussion will prompt him to give me a call.<P>I'm picking this top up later this week, I'll post up some pics later.<P>Archie||||reg||1
